Z||000000||FIEROGOD||07-11-2001||02:03 AM|||| I am going to do a caddy 4.9 swap in a 86 SE. It is a auto so i am going to use the factory fiero trans. The 4.9 is out of a 94 sedan deville. I have all of the wireing and ecm out of the caddy but i am going to use the fiero wire harness. I am using a computer out of a 91 or 92 tuned port camaro or firechicken. I will modify the fiero harness to fit the caddy motor and to plug in to the f-body ecm. I will use the factory fuel pump. The motor mounts are coming from (i think) bubba joe. Any objections or sugestions? ||||reg||1
Z||000001||JayUSA77||07-11-2001||02:07 AM||||Why are you using parts from 3 different cars. When you mix and match you start messing stuff up in my opinion.  its already hard enough to swap a engine in a fiero but to do al that too. GOOD LUCK<BR>-J<BR>literaly<P>------------------<BR>86' Black Fiero GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||00lE||07-11-2001||08:20 AM||||What a novel idea!  The 7730 ECM's have been well hacked, and are an excellent choice for an application such as this.  I am sure that there would be some code changes needed to obtain optimum performance and driveability, but this should be a piece of cake considering the fact that it is one of the most popular ECM's used to tune the F=body MAP system V8's.  Check out:<BR> <A HREF="http://www.thirdgen.org/cgi-bin/messgboard/forumdisplay.cgi?action=topics&number=10&SUBMIT=Go" TARGET=_blank>http://www.thirdgen.org/cgi-bin/messgboard/forumdisplay.cgi?action=topics&number=10&SUBMIT=Go</A> <P>It should show to be a very good resource when you get ready to tune the system up.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>||||reg||1
Z||000003||Terrybogin||07-11-2001||12:16 PM||||I have been thinking the same thing ('730 ecm) in the Caddy 4.9<BR>If you use the multi port intake for the caddy, wouldn't a 305 tuned port prom be a good starting point? This could get interesting!||||reg||1
Z||000004||terryk||07-11-2001||12:55 PM||||Doesn't the caddy engine use an Idle Speed Control solenoid rather than an Idle Air Control servo?<P>If so, then you'll need to adapt a TB with an IAC. <P>I agree, the speed density 8D code in 7727 or 7730 would be a good starting point.<P>Tuning does take some patience and knowledge but I think it would be worth the effort.<P>But before you march off and assume that any particular group (third gen, DIY-EFI, etc.) is going to help, keep in mind that many of us are nervous about helping people with tuning. The biggest issue is that your problem becomes my problem. Your melted engine is my fault. Getting it to run is one thing, but getting it to run right is another. <P>Before you start on this project, get some basic knowledge under your belt and some level of commitment from some one to help when you get to the details level.<BR><p>[This message has been edited by terryk (edited 07-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||rockcrawl||07-11-2001||04:51 PM||||I have a few comments/suggestions that may be useful.<BR> If you have the Cadillac harness, use it. It is a better match than the Fiero harness and it plugs right into the '7730. You'll need to relocate most of the pins. If you have the Cadillac PCM, throw it away, as far away as you can. Don't even bother trying to use the Caddy PCM. The PCM and IPC share info through the UART data link, and without the shared data, it will not work properly. You will not be able to read fault codes, the scanner will not make communication. I've tried. Mine runs in limp mode. For more info read up on code E047.<BR> Terryk is correct about the ISC vs. IAC. To use the '7730 you need to get rid of the Caddy MPFI throttle body and use one with a IAC. I'm experimenting with several options. A truck TBI with the injectors removed will bolt on but the EGR needs to be removed to make clearance for the IAC. I have a 75mm LS1 TB on the way, I'm going to see if I can make a plenum to bolt it onto the intake. <BR> The V6 Fiero fuel pump seems to be working fine for now. If it can't keep up, a Camaro or Caddy pump will fit in it's place.<BR>  <A HREF="http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fortunecity.com/silverstone/impala/403/cadero.htm</A> ||||reg||14
